From: SP11 sensors worker
Subject: [PATCH] hexagonrpcd: serve writable registry files for the ADSP SNS framework

The ADSP sensor framework creates and rewrites its registry under
/persist/sensors/registry/registry through FastRPC apps_std. Upstream
hexagonrpcd 0.5.0 serves every file read-only and answers write opens with
AEE_EUNSUPPORTED. This patch adds, for files below a mapped directory only:

 - open flags from the stdio mode (r, r+, w, w+, a, a+) in fopen_with_env
   (method 19) and a new fopen (method 0);
 - fwrite (method 5) and fsync (method 23);
 - fremove (method 24) as a success stub (nothing is deleted). Method
   numbers follow the order of the methods in quic/fastrpc
   idl/apps_std.idl (fopen=0 ... fsync=23, fremove=24, opendir=26,
   stat=31), which matches the IDs hexagonrpcd already uses;
 - a write unit test through the path-walking API.

Virtual directories, sysfs/socinfo mappings and DSP libraries stay
read-only. The wire layout of fwrite is derived from the IDL and by
analogy with fread; only the device can verify it.

